; DERIVED FROM THE SPRITE ART, NOT LEFT AS THE PLACEHOLDER GRAYS (the Vauban's own SP5 ruling,
; re-run here). base_0..2 hold the 2026-09-19 sprite's most-common literal fill colors: a teal-grey,
; a pale grey and a muted violet, most-used first per the Iskander's own slot convention. That
; sprite had no channel-encoded pixels, so the scheme was inert on it.
; THE 1.3.5 ART IS CHANNEL-ENCODED (measured 2026-10-11 with the same shader-literal test
; palette_swap_func.gdshaderinc uses): mf_primrose.png and mf_smilerose.png use the R, G and B
; slots, their _back views R and G. So these colours now paint the token by default, and the
; player's colour picker repaints it.
[sub_resource type="Resource" id="Resource_colorscheme"]
script = ExtResource("3_colorscheme")
base_0 = Color(0.4627451, 0.5372549, 0.56078434, 1)
base_1 = Color(0.654902, 0.7137255, 0.7294118, 1)
base_2 = Color(0.36078432, 0.28235295, 0.38039216, 1)

[sub_resource type="Resource" id="Resource_statblock"]
